WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.918
Can a caste move up?

2
00:00:01.918 --> 00:00:03.192
Srinivas said yes,

3
00:00:03.192 --> 00:00:04.900
by adopting the customs of

4
00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:06.334
higher castes.

5
00:00:06.669 --> 00:00:09.433
Ghurye listed six features of

6
00:00:09.433 --> 00:00:10.911
caste in 1932.

7
00:00:10.911 --> 00:00:15.367
Srinivas introduced Sanskritisation in 1952.

8
00:00:15.367 --> 00:00:17.740
Dumont's Homo Hierarchicus,

9
00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:18.649
in 1966,

10
00:00:18.649 --> 00:00:21.634
centred purity and pollution.

11
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.965
Sanskritisation is when a caste

12
00:00:23.965 --> 00:00:25.815
adopts the rituals and habits

13
00:00:25.815 --> 00:00:27.826
of higher castes to claim

14
00:00:27.826 --> 00:00:28.912
higher status.

15
00:00:28.912 --> 00:00:30.236
Positional change,

16
00:00:30.236 --> 00:00:31.765
not structural.

17
00:00:32.472 --> 00:00:34.208
A dominant caste has numbers

18
00:00:34.208 --> 00:00:35.237
and land,

19
00:00:35.237 --> 00:00:36.407
political power,

20
00:00:36.407 --> 00:00:38.480
and decent ritual rank.

21
00:00:38.806 --> 00:00:39.983
Your turn.

22
00:00:39.983 --> 00:00:41.870
What kind of change?
